        <item>
            <title>2.0.6</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 17:45:43 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>20006</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 2.0.6</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Pins&amp;Grid puts every pin, handle and segment label on the right spot again for vectors from Figma, SVGs and any shape layer with nested groups. Before, they could land too small and up left.</li>
  <li>On the Mac, MotionUI now has a Learn tab. Getting started ticks itself as each part starts working, and short animations show where to click: opening the panel in After Effects, running the Figma plugin, sending a frame, connecting Claude or Codex. Every guide links to the full steps and, where there is one, the After Effects project file to download.</li>
  <li>On the Mac, the setup checklists in each tab play the animation for the step you are on, and the Figma checklist starts with the MotionUI plugin from the Figma Community.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
