        <item>
            <title>2.0.5</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 16:39:43 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>20005</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 2.0.5</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Figma frames arrive in After Effects as more editable layers. Gradients with more than two stops, gradients that fade out, inner shadows, dashed strokes, stacked gradient fills, masks and strokes on single sides now come over as real layers instead of a flat image.</li>
  <li>Frames sent into a comp of another size keep their proportions, including type, corners, strokes, shadows and gradients.</li>
  <li>Claude and Codex can rename a comp, and expressions that use its name follow. They can also set its background, duration, frame rate, work area and the comp motion blur switch with shutter angle.</li>
  <li>Claude and Codex can package comps as a clean project to share: only those comps and what they use, with the footage collected next to it.</li>
  <li>The Typewriter preview in the Text tab now plays in step with the other text animations.</li>
  <li>The Figma plugin updates to version 26.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
